    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/446": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor PT - SOD Oral Maxillo Surgery (.40 FTE)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Clin Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) invites applications for one part-time Clinical Instructor position (40% FTE) in the Department of Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery. Primary responsibilities include the delivery of general anesthesia and sedation for dental patients, participation in didactic and clinical education of dental students and residents through lectures and seminars, and involvement in departmental and institutional administrative activities. In 2027, UMSOD will open a fully accredited ambulatory dental surgery center (ASC) featuring two operating rooms and three procedure rooms. The ASC will focus on comprehensive dental care for pediatric and special needs patients, as well as patients requiring oral and maxillofacial surgical procedures. Dentist anesthesiologists will play a central role in the ASC, providing direct patient care and contributing to anesthesia-related clinical and administrative operations. The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) is the world's first dental college and Maryland’s predominant provider of comprehensive and emergency oral health services for individuals of all ages, including the underserved and disadvantaged. Through research innovation, creativity, and productive partnerships, our faculty, staff, and students are developing and implementing novel approaches to advance oral health and improve lives. Qualifications Required: DDS/DMD or equivalent degree Completion of a CODA-accredited Dental Anesthesiology residency Eligibility for regular or limited licensure to practice dentistry in the State of Maryland Current board certification by the American Dental Board of Anesthesiology (ADBA), or board eligibility with attainment of diplomate status within five years of employment The Position will be available until filled. Interested applicants should go to the University of Maryland Job Portal and submit a statement of practice and career goals, a current curriculum vitae, and the names of three references. Hiring range: $54,000 - $64,000 per year (depending on academic rank and commensurate with education and experience). Primary responsibilities include the delivery of general anesthesia and sedation for dental patients, participation in didactic and clinical education of dental students and residents through lectures and seminars, and involvement in departmental and institutional administrative activities."
    },
