    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/457": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor PT - SOD Oral Maxillo Surgery (.10 FTE)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Clin Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The University of Maryland, Department of Oral-Maxillofacial Surgery, is seeking applications for 2 part-time faculty members at the rank of Clinical Instructor in the Department of Oral-Maxillofacial Surgery. There will be two positions at a 0.1 FTE (1 day per week every other week) position. Receipt of a DDS, DMD, or equivalent degree, and eligibility for licensure to practice dentistry in Maryland are required. Possession of or eligibility for a class III anesthesia permit in the State of Maryland is highly desirable. Candidates should have formal residency training in Oral Surgery/Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery. Exceptional applicants who have not completed formal residency training but possess significant oral surgery experience or preliminary training in OMFS may also be considered. Experience in undergraduate and/or postgraduate teaching is an added advantage. Interested applicants should submit the following: (1) a signed/dated detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a statement of teaching interests, and (3) four letters of recommendation into the portal. Hiring range: $13,500 - $16,000 per year (depending on rank and commensurate with education and experience). Responsibilities include academic and clinical teaching at undergraduate and residency levels, supervision of dental students, and care of patients in the Oral Maxillofacial Surgery Clinic and the Acute Care Clinic at the University of Maryland School of Dentistry and the Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Clinic at the University of Maryland Medical Centre."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/459": {
      "title": "Open Rank Assistant Professor or Associate Professor - SOD Microbial Pathogenesis",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The Department of Microbial Pathogenesis at the University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We seek an exceptional scientist with a research program focused on molecular and cellular mechanisms of disease, particularly those underlying the initiation, progression, and resolution of fungal infections. The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) is the world's first dental college and Maryland’s predominant provider of comprehensive and emergency oral health services for individuals of all ages, including the underserved and disadvantaged. Through research innovation, creativity, and productive partnerships, our faculty, staff, and students are developing and implementing novel approaches to advance oral health and improve lives. Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D., D.D.S., M.D., or equivalent degree and postdoctoral research experience. Evidence of scholarly accomplishment, innovation, and the potential to develop an internationally recognized research program is required. Please submit the following: a signed/dated detailed curriculum vitae, a statement of short and long-term research and teaching interests, and four letters of recommendation. Hiring range: $128,000 - $160,000 per year (depending on academic rank and commensurate with education and experience). Candidates whose work addresses host–fungus interactions are of special interest, especially those studying filamentous fungi or applying immunological approaches to understand pathogenic processes. We welcome applicants with expertise in fungal pathogenesis, genetics, molecular biology, innate immunology, genomics, functional genomics, systems biology, or related disciplines. Outstanding candidates working in any area broadly related to fungal disease and host responses are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain a vigorous, externally funded research program, contribute to graduate and professional education, and participate in departmental and university service activities. The candidate will join a collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment with opportunities for interaction across microbiology, immunology, infectious diseases, genomics, and cell biology. All department faculty will also be members of the Graduate Program in Life Sciences, University of Maryland Graduate School."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/475": {
      "title": "Research Associate: Pediatric Surgery",
      "description": "Category: Research JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The Department of Surgery, Division of Pediatric Surgery, at the University of Maryland School of Medicine seeks a Research Associate. Under the direction of Dr. Kimberly Lumpkins, the successful candidate will support and develop the clinical, translational, and educational research interests of the division as a core team member. Interested candidates should email their CV and two professional references to Dr. Lumpkins at klumpkins@som.umaryland.edu . The successful candidate should be able to: Cultivate scientific inquiries from initiation to completion Work collaboratively across departments and institutions Be involved in the research training of student and resident learners Effectively balance a portfolio of projects spanning several academic disciplines Qualifications Candidates must have a PhD Strong scientific writing skills are essential Prior experience with drafting IRB protocols and/or grant writing preferred Qualifications Candidates must have a PhD Strong scientific writing skills are essential Prior experience with drafting IRB protocols and/or grant writing preferred "
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/477": {
      "title": "Faculty Position: Urologic Reconstruction / Pelvic Surgery",
      "description": "Category: Healthcare JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The University of Maryland Division of Urology Seeks a Reconstructive Surgeon The Division of Urology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is recruiting for a BC/BE urologist interested in reconstructive urology. Applicants should be qualified to be appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor. Responsibilities will include clinical care of urology patients, education of students and residents and participation in research programs. Practice opportunities are available at the University of Maryland Medical Center, University of Maryland Midtown Campus, Veterans’ Affairs Maryland Health Care System (Baltimore) and other system locations to be determined. Opportunities for basic and clinical research are available for interested candidates. Preference will be given to candidates with fellowship training in genitourinary reconstructive surgery. OPPORTUNITY HIGHLIGHTS • Patient Diversity – Manage a high volume of patients with urinary incontinence, urethral strictures, ureteral strictures, as well as patients who need post radiation or post traumatic injury reconstruction. • University of Maryland is home to the renowned R Adams Cowley Shock Trauma Center — the nation’s first integrated trauma hospital and a globally recognized leader in complex trauma, reconstructive surgery, and multidisciplinary critical care. • Faculty benefit from collaboration within one of the country’s highest-volume Level I trauma systems, offering exceptional exposure to complex genitourinary reconstruction, pelvic trauma, urethral injury, and challenging referral cases. • Collaborate with Urology residents to contribute to a positive learning experience. • Collaborate with a committed clinical team, including PAs and RNs, to provide top-notch patient care. • Receive academic rank at Assistant or Associate Professor with a schedule to support research, teaching, and clinical work. COMMUNITY INFORMATION • Located in Downtown Baltimore, Maryland near the Inner Harbor • Downtown Baltimore is home to Camden Yards (Baltimore Orioles), M&T Bank Stadium (Baltimore Ravens), and the National Aquarium • Home of the Baltimore National Heritage Area, which promotes, preserves, and enhances Baltimore’s cultural and historic legacy and natural resources • Proximity to Washington, DC and Northern Virginia • Convenient train travel via Amtrak and international airport access To apply, please send your curriculum vitae and a brief statement of academic and clinical interests to: Mohummad Siddiqui, MD FACS Professor and Chief, Division of Urology 29 S. Greene St, Suite 500 Baltimore, MD, 21201 msiddiqui@som.umaryland.edu Salary Range: $312,805 - $590,430 The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the DEPARTMENTAL faculty compensation program or pay from participation in DEPARTMENTAL variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. Further information about the Department of Surgery and UMSOM can be obtained at the following websites: http://medschool.umaryland.edu/ UMB is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. We value diversity and how it enriches our academic and scientific community and strive toward cultivating an inclusive environment that supports all employees. Expected rank is Assistant Professor or higher, however, rank and tenure status is dependent on candidate’s qualifications Further information about the Department of Surgery and UMSOM can be obtained at the following websites: http://medschool.umaryland.edu/ Qualifications See above. "
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/479": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Plastic Surgery",
      "description": "Category: Healthcare JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States FACULTY POSITION: DEPARTMENT OF SURGERY, DIVISION OF PLASTIC SURGERY The University of Maryland School of Medicine is recruiting a board eligible or board certified full-time academic Plastic Surgeon to join the Division of Plastic Surgery. This role offers the opportunity to develop a comprehensive plastic surgery practice within a major academic health system, with a focus on reconstructive and aesthetic breast surgery. Microsurgery fellowship training is an asset for this position but not required for individuals with experience. This position provides the opportunity to develop an aesthetic plastic surgery practice based on candidate interests. The University of Maryland provides a broad, multidisciplinary clinical environment, with access to complex reconstruction and oncologic patients across the medical system. This position offers practice opportunities at the University of Maryland downtown campus and affiliated community hospitals, offering scheduling and site flexibility. Faculty work closely with colleagues in all facets of surgery, allowing for a diverse and stimulating practice. The position is ideally suited for a surgeon who values clinical excellence, teaching, and academic growth. Faculty will participate in the education of plastic surgery residents in our combined University of Maryland/Johns Hopkins residency program, as well as general surgery residents, fellows, and medical students. As part of a nationally recognized academic institution, faculty benefit from robust infrastructure for clinical, outcomes-based, and translational research, as well as mentorship and support for promotion and career advancement. Requirements include successful completion of an ACGME accredited training program in Plastic Surgery, BE/BC in Plastic Surgery, and ability to obtain an unrestricted Maryland State medical license. This position includes a competitive compensation and benefits package. Interested applicants should additionally send an updated curriculum vitae and brief statement of academic and clinical interests to Sara Glazer via email: skglazer@som.umaryland.edu Appointment will be at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level, and academic rank and salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Salary Range Base Compensation: $403,786 - $818,752 The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the departmental faculty compensation program or pay from participation in departmental variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs, tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. Further information about the Department of Surgery and UMSOM can be obtained at the following website: http://medschool.umaryland.edu/ UMB is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. We value diversity and how it enriches our academic and scientific community and strive toward cultivating an inclusive Qualifications See above "
