    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/432": {
      "title": "Section Chief, Colorectal Surgery",
      "description": "Category: Healthcare JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States FACULTY POSITION SECTION CHIEF OF COLORECTAL SURGERY AND SURGICAL QUALITY OFFICER DIVISION OF GENERAL SURGERY DEPARTMENT OF SURGERY The University of Maryland School of Medicine seeks candidates for the role of Section Chief of Colorectal Surgery in the Department of Surgery and Surgical Quality Officer for the University of Maryland Medical Center (UMMC). Candidates for the full-time faculty position should qualify for the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. The successful candidate will be board certified in Colorectal Surgery and have a strong academic interest in quality and safety. Responsibilities will include building a robust clinical colorectal program at UMMC and contributing to the comprehensive growth of colorectal surgery throughout the medical system, while educating medical students, surgery residents, and fellows. As Surgical Quality Officer for UMMC, the successful candidate will direct surgical quality improvement activities across all surgical subspecialties of the medical center with the direct support of the Department of Quality Improvement. The School of Medicine is located in downtown Baltimore, Maryland, near the famous Inner Harbor and Camden Yards. The University of Maryland School of Medicine offers excellent benefits and is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Interested individuals should apply, send an updated curriculum vitae and a brief statement of academic and clinical interests to: Jonathan Pearl, MD Chief, Division of General Surgery 29 South Greene Street, Suite 600 University of Maryland School of Medicine Baltimore, MD, 21201 JPearl@som.umaryland.edu Salary Range: $346,354 - $567,168 The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the DEPARTMENTAL faculty compensation program or pay from participation in DEPARTMENTAL variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. Further information about the Department of Surgery and UMSOM can be obtained at the following websites: http://medschool.umaryland.edu/ UMB is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. We value diversity and how it enriches our academic and scientific community and strive toward cultivating an inclusive environment that supports all employees. Expected rank is Assistant Professor or higher, however, rank and tenure status is dependent on candidate’s qualifications Further information about the Department of Surgery and UMSOM can be obtained at the following websites: http://medschool.umaryland.edu/ Qualifications See above. "
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/444": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Assistant/ Associate/ Professor -SOM Kahlert Institute",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The Kahlert Institute for Addiction Medicine at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is recruiting several tenure-track or tenured faculty members at the Assistant, Associate, or Professorial rank. We are interested in basic science candidates who have interests in translational addiction science. Faculty will work alongside basic and clinical research teams to contribute to the broader goal of advancing the science of addiction medicine. Specific areas of interest include (1) therapeutic development informed by mechanisms underlying drug exposure and consequences, (2) pain, (3) polysubstance exposure, (4) novel computational approaches including neural encoding and genomics, (5) gestational and developmental exposures in addiction, (6) sleep and circadian systems in addiction, and (7) stem cell-based approaches, including iPSCs and organoids. The Kahlert Institute for Addiction Medicine at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is recruiting several tenure-track or tenured faculty members at the Assistant, Associate, or Professorial rank. The candidates’ research program must be aligned with the mission of the Kahlert Institute for Addiction Medicine, which is dedicated to transforming addiction research, prevention, treatment, and education across the State of Maryland and advancing the science of addiction medicine more broadly. The Institute is located in the new HSF III building, which offers state-of-the-art wet lab facilities. This search is targeted toward wet lab researchers, and candidates' research programs must be able to make use of these facilities. The new hires will have an appointment in a basic or clinical department at the University of Maryland School of Medicine , but will be affiliated with and housed in the Kahlert Institute for Addiction Medicine. We offer highly competitive salary and recruitment packages. The University of Maryland, Baltimore is an R1 research institution with a vibrant community of leaders in the fields of addiction and neuroscience research across several departments including Psychiatry ; Neurobiology ; and Pharmacology, Physiology, and Drug Development . The hired faculty will be immersed in a highly collaborative environment with dynamic and productive research programs and initiatives , state-of-the-art equipment, and outstanding core facilities . Opportunities for mentoring and training the next generation of scientists are available through the Graduate Program in Life Sciences and MSTP program, including the Graduate Program in Neuroscience . Ample professional development resources and support for faculty are readily available. Candidates should submit , as a single PDF: (1) cover letter; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) statement of research interests and vision (3-page maximum); (4) brief statement of translational research vision including current or future research ; (5) brief service statement that addresses the mission, vision, and values of the University of Maryland ; and (6) contact information for three references. Applications will be accepted until all positions are filled. UMB is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. We encourage applications from a broad range of applicants with diverse backgrounds and life experiences that may bring new perspectives to biomedical research, including but not limited to lived experiences and perspectives on race, religion, national origin, sex, gender identity of expression, physical or mental disability, or socio-economic backgrounds, among others. If you need a reasonable accommodation for a disability, for any part of the recruitment process, please contact us at https://www.umaryland.edu/jobs/ and let us know the nature of your request and your contact information. Please note that only inquiries concerning a request for reasonable accommodation will be responded to from this address. Salary Range Assistant Professor: $116,000 - $140,000 Associate Professor: $140,000 - $160, 000 Professor: $174,000 - $228,000 The University of Maryland School of Medicine (SOM) was chartered in 1807 as the first public medical school in the United States. It continues today as one of the fastest growing, top-tier biomedical research enterprises in the world. SOM is dedicated to providing excellence in biomedical education, basic and clinical research, quality patient care and service to improve the health of the citizens of Maryland and beyond. We are interested in basic science candidates with a terminal degree (e.g. Ph.D., M.D., Pharm.D.) who have interests in translational addiction science. Faculty will work alongside basic and clinical research teams to contribute to the broader goal of advancing the science of addiction medicine. Our group has strong basic science expertise in the circuit and behavioral mechanisms of addiction, and we are looking to complement and expand beyond this core strength. S pecific areas of interest include (1) therapeutic development informed by mechanisms underlying drug exposure and consequences, (2) pain, (3) polysubstance exposure, (4) novel computational approaches including neural encoding and genomics, (5) gestational and developmental exposures in addiction, (6) sleep and circadian systems in addiction, and (7) stem cell-based approaches, including iPSCs and organoids. The appointee ordinarily shall have established an outstanding record of teaching and research, scholarship or creative performance, and, where appropriate to the mission of the institution, a national reputation. There shall be continuing evidence of relevant and effective service to the institution, the community, and the profession."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/462": {
      "title": "Faculty: Cardiac Surgeon",
      "description": "Category: Healthcare JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States FACULTY POSITION: DEPARTMENT OF SURGERY, DIVISION OF CARDIAC SURGERY The University of Maryland School of Medicine is seeking candidates to join the full-time faculty of the Division of Cardiac Surgery. This role is comprehensive and requires individuals who are board-certified in Cardiothoracic Surgery or have completed training in an accredited Cardiothoracic Surgery residency or fellowship program. Responsibilities will include establishing a broad Cardiac Surgery practice at the University of Maryland Medical Center, conducting independent clinical or laboratory research, providing care to complex cardiac surgery patients at the Downtown Campus, contributing to the comprehensive growth of cardiac surgery throughout the Medical System, and educating medical students, surgery residents, and fellows. We are looking for candidates who have a clear plan for clinical practice building, academic development, and scholarly activity that is consistent with the mission of the University of Maryland School of Medicine. Faculty will have the privilege and responsibility of teaching all facets of cardiac surgery to integrated thoracic surgery trainees. They will expand their research and scholarly activities to achieve national and international recognition as they advance the field. The University of Maryland is a world-renowned research institution that provides a superb academic foundation for basic, clinical, and translational research. Robust opportunities exist to enhance the Division’s existing research portfolio through collaboration with various researchers within the Department of Surgery and across the University. About the Division: The Division of Cardiac Surgery at the University of Maryland School of Medicine includes 10 clinical faculty providing cardiac surgery services at three locations and is the market leader in cardiac surgical care in the State of Maryland. The Division sponsors a mature, integrated 6-year Cardiothoracic Training program and a Cardiothoracic Fellowship. The Division is home to several NIH-funded surgeon-scientists, has a Clinical Research Unit with over 40 prospectively enrolling clinical trials, and is a site for the NHLBI-sponsored Cardiothoracic Surgical Trials Network. The University of Maryland School of Medicine is located in downtown Baltimore, Maryland, near the famous Inner Harbor and Camden Yards. It offers a full package of benefits and is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Interested individuals should apply and send an updated curriculum vitae and a brief statement of academic and clinical interests to: James M. Brown, MD Chief, Division of Cardiac Surgery 22 South Greene Street University of Maryland School of Medicine Baltimore, MD, 21201 JMBrown@som.umaryland.edu Salary Range: $690,750 - $1,173,827 The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the DEPARTMENTAL faculty compensation program or pay from participation in DEPARTMENTAL variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. Further information about the Department of Surgery and UMSOM can be obtained at the following websites: http://medschool.umaryland.edu/ Qualifications See above. "
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/491": {
      "title": "Open Rank Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor -SOD Comprehensive Dentistry (163727)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States Assistant Group Practice Director (0.8 FTE) Open Rank: Clinical Instructor / Clinical Assistant Professor University of Maryland School of Dentistry Department of Comprehensive Dentistry Division of General Practice Position Overview The University of Maryland School of Dentistry invites applications for a 0.8 full-time equivalent (FTE) clinical faculty position as Assistant Group Practice Director in the Department of Comprehensive Dentistry, Division of General Practice. There are two 0.80 FTE positions available. We are seeking an enthusiastic, collaborative dentist who is passionate about patient care, enjoys sharing clinical knowledge, and is interested in helping educate the next generation of dental professionals. This position offers an opportunity to combine clinical teaching, student mentorship, comprehensive patient care, and professional development within an academic environment that values innovation, collaboration, and clinical excellence. Dentists transitioning from private practice to academia are encouraged to apply. Your clinical experience and practical knowledge can make a meaningful difference in preparing dental students for independent practice. Previous academic teaching experience is not required. We will support your transition into dental education through mentorship from experienced faculty, faculty development programs, training in clinical teaching and student assessment, and opportunities to participate in curriculum development, digital dentistry education, and educational research. Faculty members will also have opportunities to develop scholarly projects, present at professional conferences, and build an academic portfolio toward faculty promotion. This position offers a pathway to grow from an experienced dentist into a confident dental educator. Academic rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. About the Position The Division of General Practice follows a comprehensive care group practice model designed to prepare students for independent clinical practice. The division consists of eight group practices, each serving approximately 32 third- and fourth-year dental students under the guidance of two faculty practice leaders. The Assistant Group Practice Director will work collaboratively with the Group Practice Director, clinical faculty, and patient care coordinators to support student learning, comprehensive patient care, and effective clinical operations. The successful candidate will play an important role in helping students develop clinical competence, sound professional judgment, confidence, and accountability in delivering patient-centered care. Required Qualifications DDS, DMD, or equivalent dental degree. Eligibility for an appropriate Maryland dental license or faculty teaching license. Clinical experience in comprehensive general dentistry, including diagnosis, treatment planning, direct and indirect restorative procedures, and patient management. Ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and patients. Commitment to evidence-based clinical practice, patient-centered care, and dental education. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively within an interdisciplinary clinical environment. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and professional communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Completion of an Advanced Education in General Dentistry (AEGD) or General Practice Residency (GPR) program, or equivalent advanced clinical experience. Experience mentoring dental students, residents, or early-career dentists. Interest in clinical teaching, digital dentistry, contemporary restorative procedures, and educational innovation. Experience in comprehensive patient management and interdisciplinary treatment planning. Interest in educational scholarship, clinical research, curriculum development, or academic leadership. Why Join the University of Maryland School of Dentistry? The University of Maryland School of Dentistry offers an opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the dental profession while continuing to grow professionally as a clinician and educator. Our department values collaboration, mentorship, clinical excellence, and the development of future academic leaders. Faculty members have opportunities to: Develop as dental educators: Learn effective clinical teaching, student assessment, and mentoring approaches through faculty development and guidance from experienced academic colleagues. Advance clinically: Remain engaged with comprehensive patient care, contemporary restorative dentistry, digital workflows, and interdisciplinary treatment planning. Participate in educational innovation: Contribute to curriculum development, digital dentistry initiatives, clinical simulation, and new approaches to dental education. Build an academic portfolio: Explore educational scholarship, clinical research, scholarly presentations, and collaborative projects aligned with individual interests. Grow professionally: Receive guidance in academic career planning, faculty promotion, and the development of leadership skills. Make a lasting impact: Help dental students transition from supervised learning to confident, competent, and independent clinical practice. Hiring range: $110,000 - $116,000 (depending on academic rank and commensurate with education and experience). Key Responsibilities Clinical Teaching and Student Mentorship Provide direct clinical supervision, instruction, and constructive feedback to predoctoral dental students delivering comprehensive patient care. Mentor students in diagnosis, phased treatment planning, clinical decision-making, restorative dentistry, and interdisciplinary patient management. Support students in developing clinical competence, critical thinking, professional judgment, communication skills, and confidence in independent patient care. Monitor student clinical progress and collaborate with the Group Practice Director to identify learning needs, provide feedback, and support achievement of clinical competencies. Promote evidence-based dentistry, ethical practice, patient safety, and professional accountability. Support the integration of contemporary clinical techniques, digital dentistry, and emerging technologies into student learning. Comprehensive Patient Care and Group Practice Operations Collaborate with the Group Practice Director and patient care coordinators to support continuity, quality, and timely delivery of comprehensive dental care. Assist students with patient management, interdisciplinary treatment planning, specialty referrals, and urgent dental care. Support coordination of patient assignments, treatment sequencing, and clinical scheduling within the group practice. Assist in identifying and addressing challenges related to patient care, student progress, and clinical operations. Participate in initiatives to improve clinical efficiency, patient experiences, and educational outcomes. Contribute to quality assurance, patient safety, and continuous improvement activities. Academic Engagement and Faculty Development Participate in faculty development programs, clinical calibration, and educational activities. Contribute to the improvement of clinical teaching methods, student assessment, and educational resources. Participate in curriculum development and initiatives related to contemporary dental education. Engage in scholarly, educational, or professional activities appropriate to academic rank, individual interests, and assigned effort. Collaborate with faculty across clinical disciplines and dental specialties. Participate in departmental and School of Dentistry service activities appropriate to the appointment. Appointment and Work Schedule This is a 0.8 FTE clinical faculty appointment , with responsibilities proportional to the appointment. The position will primarily focus on clinical teaching, student mentorship, and supporting group practice operations. The Assistant Group Practice Director will work collaboratively with the Group Practice Director rather than serving as the primary administrator responsible for overall group practice operations. Specific clinical schedules and responsibilities will be determined in consultation with the Division Director and Department Chair. Opportunities for faculty practice, additional teaching, educational scholarship, and professional development may be incorporated based on faculty interests, institutional needs, and approved effort allocation."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/490": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor PT - SOD Oral Maxillo Surgery (.40 FTE)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Clin Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The University of Maryland, Department of Oral-Maxillofacial Surgery, is seeking applications for two part-time faculty members at the rank of Clinical Instructor in the Department of Oral-Maxillofacial Surgery. There will be one position at a 0.2 FTE (1 day per week) and one position as a 0.4 FTE (2 days per week). The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) is the world's first dental college and Maryland’s predominant provider of comprehensive and emergency oral health services for individuals of all ages, including the underserved and disadvantaged. Through research innovation, creativity, and productive partnerships, our faculty, staff, and students are developing and implementing novel approaches to advance oral health and improve lives. Receipt of a DDS, DMD, or equivalent degree, and eligibility for licensure to practice dentistry in Maryland are required. Possession of or eligibility for a class III anesthesia permit in the State of Maryland is highly desirable. Candidates should have formal residency training in Oral Surgery/Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery. Exceptional applicants who have not completed formal residency training but possess significant oral surgery experience or preliminary training in OMFS may also be considered. Experience in undergraduate and/or postgraduate teaching is an added advantage. Hiring range: $32,000 - $64,000 per year (depending on rank and commensurate with education and experience). Interested applicants should submit the following: (1) a signed/dated detailed curriculum vitae, (2) a statement of teaching interests, and (3) four letters of recommendation. Responsibilities include academic and clinical teaching at undergraduate and residency levels, supervision of dental students, and care of patients in the Oral Maxillofacial Surgery Clinic and the Acute Care Clinic at the University of Maryland School of Dentistry and the Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Clinic at the University of Maryland Medical Center."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/382": {
      "title": "Non-Adjunct Faculty - SOM Diagnostic Radiology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Adjunct Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The Department of Diagnostic Radiology and Nuclear Medicine at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is seeking Pediatric radiologists. Under new leadership, the Department is undergoing a dynamic transformation, building on its longstanding legacy of clinical excellence. We offer a highly competitive compensation plan with performance-based incentives, along with a strong emphasis on schedule flexibility and faculty support. Aware of the marketplace challenges in pediatric radiology, the Department is offering new and creative schedule options with a range of compensation opportunities. Relatively low clinical volume: < 35 wRVUs/shift, and < 25 wRVUs/shift on weekends. Option 1: 2 weeks on and 1 week off 190 total clinical shifts per year. 170 weekday shifts per year (8a-5p) structured as 2 weeks of 5-day workweeks (4 days onsite, 1 day remote) followed by the 3 rd week off; translates to 17 weeks off duty per year! 10 weekends of call per year (remote from home; 20 total shifts). Base salary : $550,000 – $650,000 ( based on rank and experience ) Opportunity to pick up extra shifts for additional compensation Option 2: 26-week model 150 total clinical shifts per year. 130 weekday shifts per year (8a-5p); 26 5-day workweeks; 26 weeks off duty per year! Every other duty week can be done remotely from home 10 weekends of call per year (remote from home; 20 total shifts). Base salary : ~$425,000 (based on rank and experience) Opportunity to pick up extra shifts for additional compensation Option 3: Higher salary (with option for pediatric radiology leadership) 220 total clinical shifts per year; 10 weeks off duty 40 5-day workweeks (200 weekday shifts) 20 weekend shifts per year (10 full weekends) 25% of weekday work can be remote from home; all weekend work can be remote. Base salary : $675k (based on rank and experience) We invite part-time applicants to apply for prorated work and salaries! Additional Benefits $25,000 signing bonus Comprehensive benefits package Generous retirement contributions Robust family and medical leave policies Academic appointment commensurate with experience For more details, please enquire by email and attach your CV: tarek.hanna@umm.edu The University of Maryland, Baltimore is an Equal Opportunity, Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. We value diversity and how it enriches our academic and scientific community and strive toward cultivating an inclusive environment that supports all employees. Expertise in the discipline and recognition for accomplishment sufficient to gain the endorsement of the preponderance of the members of the faculty of the department to which he or she is appointed. faculty members at the University who are: Appointed to provide contractually defined responsibilities such as research, service, or instruction for non-credit bearing courses; Neither tenured nor eligible for tenure;"
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/414": {
      "title": "Open Rank Assistant or Associate Professor - SOD Operative Dentistry & Cariology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States Full-time Assistant or Associate Professor, Cariology & Operative Dentistry, Department of Comprehensive Dentistry The University of Maryland School of Dentistry invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track faculty position Assistant or Associate Professor in the Division of Operative Dentistry& Cariology, Department of Comprehensive Dentistry. We are seeking dynamic, enthusiastic candidates with a strong commitment to dental education and a collaborative spirit. Ideal applicants will demonstrate a positive attitude toward teaching and a desire to grow professionally within academic dentistry. The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) is the world's first dental college and Maryland’s predominant provider of comprehensive and emergency oral health services for individuals of all ages, including the underserved and disadvantaged. Through research innovation, creativity, and productive partnerships, our faculty, staff, and students are developing and implementing novel approaches to advance oral health and improve lives. Candidates with operative dentistry residency, master's, or Ph.D. degrees in a related content area, strong record of publications and scientific accomplishment, and dental educational research experience. Ability to provide evidence of excellent university-level teaching and significant publications An understanding of initial considerations for restoration of single-tooth edentulism via implant dentistry and clinical experience with digital dentistry applications and workflow to include intraoral image acquisition and CAD/CAM of single-tooth restorations. The position will be available until filled. Please submit the following, (1) a signed/dated detailed curriculum vitae and (2) a statement of teaching interests into the portal. Hiring range: $135,000 - $165,000 per year (depending on academic rank and commensurate with education and experience). What you can expect from University of Maryland School of Dentistry: Annual patient volumes between 25K – 30K A competitive annual salary Medical, dental and vision insurance Retirement plans Generous paid vacation, sick time, holidays and personal days An academic appointment with the University of Maryland School of Dentistry The successful candidate will contribute significantly to both preclinical and clinical instruction in Operative Dentistry. Approximately 60-80% of the role will be dedicated to teaching, with the remaining time allocated to scholarly activities, service, and professional development. Key Duties Include: Teaching preclinical and clinical courses in restorative dentistry, with a focus on operative dentistry for DDS students. Serving as course director and instructor for one or more core or elective courses, including course development and student mentoring. Supporting student learning, development, and decision-making to promote academic success and well-being. Collaborating with faculty to enhance teaching strategies and improve student outcomes. Participating in scholarly activities within and beyond the department. Engaging in departmental, school, and university committees, meetings, and community service. Maintaining a professional development plan that includes research or other scholarly pursuits. Conducting or contributing to dental research initiatives. Supervising undergraduate or graduate student research projects as needed. Demonstrating innovation in curriculum development and/or continuing education. Contributing to the professional community through peer review, grant panels, and participation in national/international conferences. Exhibiting strong interpersonal, leadership, and organizational skills, with a clear commitment to teaching and scholarship. Responding to assignments from the Chair of Comprehensive Dentistry and the Dean of the School of Dentistry to support departmental and school operations. Demonstrating teamwork in planning, problem-solving, and decision-making."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/559": {
      "title": "School Assistant Professor (Ambulatory Care) - Practice, Sciences, and Health Outcomes Research",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: School Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The University of Maryland School of Pharmacy is conducting an open search for an Assistant Professor (Ambulatory Car), Non-Tenure Track in the Department of Practice, Science, and Health Outcomes Research (P-SHOR). This position requires teaching, service to the school, campus, and the profession, scholarly activity, and the ability to establish and operate a successful clinical practice in an ambulatory care setting. The position is a full-time, non-tenure-track, 12-month appointment based at our Baltimore campus. The University of Maryland, Baltimore campus houses schools of Pharmacy, Medicine, Nursing, Social Work, Law, and Dentistry. The University of Maryland enjoys an excellent established record of accomplishment of successful collaboration for interprofessional practice and research collaborations with the other professional schools on campus. SUPERVISORY CONTROLS This position is responsible to the Chair of the Department with clinical reporting responsibility to the pharmacy director or designee at the practice site. UMB CORE VALUES Respect & Integrity, Well-Being & Sustainability, Equity & Justice, and Innovation & Discovery Established in 1841, the University of Maryland School of Pharmacy (UMSOP) is the fourth oldest school of pharmacy in the United States. As a leader in pharmacy education, scientific discovery, patient care, and community engagement; the School conducts cutting-edge research and engages in a wide variety of professional practice activities to improve the health and well-being of citizens in the state of Maryland and beyond. Doctor of Pharmacy degree from an ACPE accredited school of pharmacy. Two years of post-graduate training (residency, fellowship or equivalent experience) and teaching experience. Eligibility for certification as Ambulatory Care Pharmacy Specialist and Maryland licensure are required. Excellent communication and patient skills are essential. Candidates with specialty certification, evidence of scholarship, and several years of experience are highly desirable. A more specific delineation of responsibilities follows. REQUIRED, SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE, AND ABILITIES Professional conduct in all dealings with students, faculty, or administration. Communications - Knowledge of communication and dissemination techniques and methods. This includes alternative ways to inform via written, oral, and visual media. Education - Knowledge of principles and methods for curriculum design principles, evidence-based teaching and instruction for individuals and groups, and knowledge of measurement and assessment. Initiative - Willing and able to take on responsibilities and challenges. Leadership - Willing and able to lead; take charge and offer opinions and direction. Learning Strategies - Selecting and using instructional methods and procedures appropriate in the discipline family when learning or teaching new things. Strong interpersonal abilities with excellent verbal and written communication skills to effectively communicate with students, staff, faculty. Monitoring - Monitoring/assessing curricula to make improvements or take corrective action. Stress Tolerance - Ability to accept criticism and deal calmly and effectively with high stress situations. HOW TO APPLY Interested candidates must apply online through the Careers at UMB website and submit an initial application that includes a letter of intent (reference position number 05-179-111), curriculum vitae (signed and dated), statement of teaching philosophy, statement of scholarly interests, and names and contact information of at least three references. Shortlisted candidates will be required to submit three letters of recommendation from reviewers external to the University of Maryland School of Pharmacy. In addition to applying online, interested candidates may also send application materials to Dr. Congdon, Chair of the Faculty Search Committee: Heather Congdon, PharmD, CDCES, FNAP Professor University of Maryland School of Pharmacy Department of Practice, Sciences, and Health Outcomes Research Email: hcongdon@rx.umaryland.edu SALARY RANGE Assistant Professor: $120,000 - $140,000 The salary will be commensurate with education, experience, and qualifications. Employees whose job duties require them to work in a clinical setting or at clinical or field sites continue to be subject to the vaccine requirements of those sites. For additional information on protocols and exemptions, please visit the COVID-19 website . UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over four weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at participating University System of Maryland schools. For more information, please visit HR Benefits at https://www.umaryland.edu/hr/benefits-and-well-being/ For information regarding UMB Employee Perks, please visit https://www.umaryland.edu/hr/benefits-and-well-being/benefits-programs-and-perks/ EDUCATION Ability to teach a broad range of topics related to therapeutics and patient care. Teaching responsibilities will be determined in discussions with Vice Chair for Academic Affairs. Provide pathophysiology and pharmacotherapeutics instruction in PharmD didactic courses. Develop, teach, and participate instruction related to ambulatory care and/or community pharmacy practice in the Pharmacy Practice Laboratory experiences at the Baltimore and Shady Grove campuses. Develop and teach introductory and advanced practices experiences for pharmacy students and residents at the practice site. Provide clinical education in pharmacotherapeutics and ambulatory care topics to students, pharmacy residents, pharmacists, staff, physicians, patients, and patient caregivers. PRACTICE Develop an active clinical practice in an ambulatory care setting. Function as liaison between the school and the practice site(s). SCHOLARSHIP Engage in scholarly activity in areas of interest. Scholarship is broadly interpreted and may include the development of innovative pharmacy practices, evaluation of therapeutic outcomes, and implementation and assessment of novel instructional methods. Scholarly activity is required; publication and presentation of work is expected. Scholarly activity may be pursued either independently or in collaboration with other schools, departments, or campus faculty. Effort devoted to scholarship is expected to grow as practice becomes established. SERVICE TO THE UNIVERSITY, SCHOOL, AND PUBLIC Participate in appropriate faculty activities (e.g., faculty assembly, department meetings, and faculty committees), professional organizations, and other endeavors is also expected."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/514": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - SOM Psych Consultation LiaiSON",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/06/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The University of Maryland Medical Center, the flagship teaching hospital of the University of Maryland School of Medicine, is seeking a Consultation-Liaison psychiatrist. Both inpatient and outpatient service opportunities are available, with opportunities to develop a focus in one of several specialties. The successful candidate will receive an academic appointment at the University of Maryland School of Medicine commensurate with the school’s appointment and promotion processes. Responsibilities associated with this opportunity include: • Work as a member of an established, respected team of psychiatric consultants in a 700+ bed medical center, providing consultation to medical, surgical, and emergency department services, including the Level I Shock Trauma Center. • Duties also include: working as an inpatient attending at our downtown main campus which comprises three inpatient services with shared attending coverage as well as coverage at our nearby Midtown Campus. • Inpatient consultation is primarily a teaching service, with trainees at the medical student, resident, and Consultation-Liaison Psychiatry fellow levels. • Extensive opportunities for program development and research, with readily available mentoring. • Base salary according to qualifications and University guidelines, with up to 15% additional compensation available through over practice. • Weekend duties limited to four times per year; no call requirements. Important Benefits to highlight: • Excellent leave, vacation, and retirement benefits, including malpractice coverage. • Eligibility to apply for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program. Consultation-Liaison Psychiatry at the University of Maryland Medical Center We also provide dedicated outpatient consultation to organ transplantation, oncology, virology, and endocrinology, with expansion anticipated in some of these areas. We have a well-established Consultation-Liaison Psychiatry Fellowship program. This position carries a faculty appointment at the University and offers exciting opportunities for clinical care, teaching, and research. Academic rank and salary are commensurate with experience. The expected rank is Assistant Professor or higher; however, rank and tenure status are dependent on the candidate’s qualifications. The referenced salary range reflects base pay for an Assistant Professor, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the department’s faculty compensation program or pay from participation in department variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good-faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate’s geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training, and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. The University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB) offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position offers a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes more than four weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, and unlimited accrual of sick time. Additional benefits include comprehensive health insurance, professional learning and development programs, and tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. Note: Leave and tuition benefits are prorated for part-time employees. Needed Qualifications: Board certification in psychiatry; board eligibility in Consultation-Liaison Psychiatry; Maryland medical licensure. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to applicants who have successfully completed a fellowship in Consultation-Liaison Psychiatry in an ACGME-accredited program. Additionally, consideration will be given to applicants who have not completed a fellowship but have a minimum of two years of attending-level experience in Consultation-Liaison Psychiatry after completing an adult psychiatry residency. Doctorate or recognized terminal degree in the field of specialization. Shown potential for superior teaching, service, and research, scholarship, or r creative performance, commensurate with the mission of the UMB. May require unrestricted license in the State of Maryland. Collaborate with Consultation-Liaison psychiatrists to develop comprehensive behavioral treatment plans for patients. Participate in education of trainees within the School of Medicine, in both didactic and clinical settings. Assist with development and execution of research activities within the Consultation-Liaison Division and in collaboration with other entities within and outside the Department of Psychiatry. Perform, as needed, inpatient and outpatient treatment and diagnostic evaluations and/or specialized testing of patients in the services of the Consultation-Liaison Division. The duties will include inpatient and outpatient consultation at Downtown and Midtown medical campuses. Potential outpatient duties include Solid Organ Transplant, Thrive Clinic (IHV The appointee should also show potential for superior teaching, service, and research, scholarship, or creative performance, commensurate with the mission of the institution."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/556": {
      "title": "Open Rank Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Dentistry Orthodontics (309292)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Clin Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States University of Maryland, Baltimore, School of Dentistry is seeking to fill a position for a full-time, non-tenure track Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor Position in the Division of Orthodontics, Department of Orthodontics and Pediatric Dentistry, University of Maryland Baltimore, School of Dentistry. The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) is the world's first dental college and Maryland’s predominant provider of comprehensive and emergency oral health services for individuals of all ages, including the underserved and disadvantaged. Through research innovation, creativity, and productive partnerships, our faculty, staff, and students are developing and implementing novel approaches to advance oral health and improve lives. Requirements for the position include DDS/DMD or foreign equivalent, certificate in Orthodontics, experience in Orthodontic Education in the US, and the candidate should be preferably ABO certified/board eligible. The position will be available until filled. Interested applicants should submit the following: (1) a signed/dated detailed curriculum vitae, and (2) two letters of recommendation. Hiring Range: $140,000 - $160,000 (Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience). Responsibilities include mainly didactic and clinical teaching of Orthodontic residents, dental students, and conducting scholarly activities, participation in faculty practice, and service to the organization."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/561": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position - SOM Anesthesiology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States Advance your career in the Maryland/DC region! We invite you to join our team of multispecialty anesthesiologists at the University of Maryland. We’re seeking board-eligible/board-certified MD/DO anesthesiologists to support our rapidly expanding growth in both OR and non-OR environments. Opportunities are available within the Divisions of Adult Multispecialty Anesthesiology, Cardiothoracic Anesthesiology, Critical Care Anesthesiology, Neurosurgical Anesthesiology, Obstetric Anesthesiology, Pediatric Anesthesiology, Regional Anesthesiology and Acute Pain Medicine, and Transplant Anesthesiology, as well as our community practices at the University of Maryland Medical Center Midtown Campus and the University of Maryland Rehabilitation & Orthopaedic Institute. Duties include clinical care and teaching of learners at all levels including SRNAs, medical students, residents, and fellows. Our team is dedicated to helping faculty obtain outstanding skills and additional certifications in ultrasound, simulation, quality/safety/clinical research, and many other disciplines. Our department has a very strong research profile (#10 national 2023 Blue Ridge Ranking) as well as a perioperative data warehouse with resources to facilitate clinical research. We also offer excellent benefits (including tuition remission for both faculty and dependents), loan forgiveness, competitive compensation, and ample opportunities for academic growth and advancement. The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the Department of Anesthesiology faculty compensation program or pay from participation in Department of Anesthesiology incentive compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. For immediate consideration, please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae and contact information of three references via this online application. For additional questions after application, please contact: David Mintz, MD, PhD, Chairman, Department of Anesthesiology, University of Maryland School of Medicine, 22 South Greene Street, S11C00, Baltimore, MD 21201 - - Office Phone: 410-328-9837 - - dmintz@som.umaryland.edu The University of Maryland School of Medicine (SOM) was chartered in 1807 as the first public medical school in the United States. It continues today as one of the fastest growing, top-tier biomedical research enterprises in the world. SOM is dedicated to providing excellence in biomedical education, basic and clinical research, quality patient care and service to improve the health of the citizens of Maryland and beyond. Candidates must be ABA certified (or eligible). Doctorate or recognized terminal degree in the field of specialization. Demonstrated a degree of excellence experience in teaching, clinical or professional practice in a field of specialization establish an outstanding regional and national reputation among colleagues. Appointees shall also have demonstrated extraordinary scholarly competence and leadership in the profession. Unrestricted license in the State of Maryland. "
