nd beyond. Must be board-eligible or board-certified. Doctorate or recognized terminal degree in the field of specialization. Shown potential for superior teaching, service, and research, scholarship, or r creative performance, commensurate with the mission of the UMB. May require unrestricted license in the State of Maryland. The appointee should also show potential for superior teaching, service, and research, scholarship, or creative performance, commensurate with the mission of the institution."
