    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/573": {
      "title": "Open Rank Clinical Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor - SOD Diagnostic Sciences (248824)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Clin Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States Director of the PLUS Program, Department of Oncology and Diagnostic Sciences, Dental Clinics of UMB (Baltimore, MD) The University of Maryland School of Dentistry invites applicants to apply for full-time Open Rank Clinical Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor, non-tenure track 100% FTE faculty position in the Department of Oncology and Diagnostic Sciences. The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) is the world's first dental college and Maryland’s predominant provider of comprehensive and emergency oral health services for individuals of all ages, including the underserved and disadvantaged. Through research innovation, creativity, and productive partnerships, our faculty, staff, and students are developing and implementing novel approaches to advance oral health and improve lives. DMD, DDS from a Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) accredited institution or foreign equivalent dental degree. Candidates must possess high ethical standards, outstanding clinical skills, excellent interpersonal communication and written skills, and a record of building consensus in an academic setting. Eligibility for dental licensure in Maryland. Previous grant management experience and administration of a public health dental clinical program is preferred. This individual must be able to respond to requests with accuracy, reliability and flexibility quickly; this will often include multi-tasking patient, staff and student affairs. Proficiency in the practice of all disciplines of general dentistry, including, management and operation of a dental practice, and experience in successfully working with students. Hiring range: $137,000 - $150,000 (depending on academic rank and commensurate with education and experience). The Director of the PLUS Program of the University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD), is a full-time faculty member who will provide leadership and supervision of all educational and clinical activities of UMSOD patients living with HIV disease eligible for oral health care through the Ryan White Grants funding support. The Director will also serve as a clinician, well-versed in dental care for these medically complex patients, providing a full range of comprehensive dentistry services in this unique population as per the Ryan White Standards of Care and UMSOD/PLUS Clinic’s Ryan White oral health care work plan. The Director works with the UMSOD’s Office of Extramural Clinical Practices, Clinical Affairs, Academic Affairs, and in collaboration with the Chair of the Department of Oncology and Diagnostic Sciences to support all UMSOD programs and initiatives. Additionally, the Director works closely with local, state, and regional AIDS Service Organizations (ASO) to provide information and services related to the UMSOD/PLUS Program."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/579": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - 10419060-SOM Cardiac Surgery",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States FACULTY POSITION: DEPARTMENT OF SURGERY, DIVISION OF CARDIAC SURGERY The University of Maryland School of Medicine is seeking candidates to join the full-time faculty of the Division of Cardiac Surgery. This role is comprehensive and requires individuals who are board-certified in Cardiothoracic Surgery or have completed training in an accredited Cardiothoracic Surgery residency or fellowship program. Responsibilities will include establishing a broad Cardiac Surgery practice at the University of Maryland Medical Center, conducting independent clinical or laboratory research, providing care to complex cardiac surgery patients at the Downtown Campus, contributing to the comprehensive growth of cardiac surgery throughout the Medical System, and educating medical students, surgery residents, and fellows. We are looking for candidates who have a clear plan for clinical practice building, academic development, and scholarly activity that is consistent with the mission of the University of Maryland School of Medicine. Faculty will have the privilege and responsibility of teaching all facets of cardiac surgery to integrated thoracic surgery trainees. They will expand their research and scholarly activities to achieve national and international recognition as they advance the field. The University of Maryland is a world-renowned research institution that provides a superb academic foundation for basic, clinical, and translational research. Robust opportunities exist to enhance the Division’s existing research portfolio through collaboration with various researchers within the Department of Surgery and across the University. About the Division: The Division of Cardiac Surgery at the University of Maryland School of Medicine includes 10 clinical faculty providing cardiac surgery services at three locations and is the market leader in cardiac surgical care in the State of Maryland. The Division sponsors a mature, integrated 6-year Cardiothoracic Training program and a Cardiothoracic Fellowship. The Division is home to several NIH-funded surgeon-scientists, has a Clinical Research Unit with over 40 prospectively enrolling clinical trials, and is a site for the NHLBI-sponsored Cardiothoracic Surgical Trials Network. The University of Maryland School of Medicine is located in downtown Baltimore, Maryland, near the famous Inner Harbor and Camden Yards. It offers a full package of benefits and is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Interested individuals should send an updated curriculum vitae and a brief statement of academic and clinical interests to: James M. Brown, MD Chief, Division of Cardiac Surgery 22 South Greene Street University of Maryland School of Medicine Baltimore, MD, 21201 JMBrown@som.umaryland.edu Salary Range: $690,750 - $1,173,827 The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the DEPARTMENTAL faculty compensation program or pay from participation in DEPARTMENTAL variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. Further information about the Department of Surgery and UMSOM can be obtained at the following websites: http://medschool.umaryland.edu/ Doctorate or recognized terminal degree in the field of specialization. Shown potential for superior teaching, service, and research, scholarship, or r creative performance, commensurate with the mission of the UMB. May require unrestricted license in the State of Maryland. The appointee should also show potential for superior teaching, service, and research, scholarship, or creative performance, commensurate with the mission of the institution."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/580": {
      "title": "Path-Trained Dermatopathologist -SOM Dermatology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/11/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The University of Maryland School of Medicine, Department of Dermatology is seeking an exceptional Pathology-Trained Dermatopathologist to join our growing academic faculty. The University of Maryland School of Medicine, Department of Dermatology is seeking an exceptional Pathology-Trained Dermatopathologist to join our growing academic faculty. This is an exciting opportunity for a pathology-trained physician who has completed fellowship training in dermatopathology and is looking to build or advance a rewarding career within a highly collaborative academic dermatology environment. Expected rank for this position will be Assistant Professor or higher, however, final rank and tenure status will be commensurate with selected candidate’s experience. More than simply filling a position, we are looking for a colleague who wants to help shape and grow dermatopathology at the University of Maryland. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to bring their expertise in pathology and dermatopathology to a department committed to outstanding diagnostic care, education, collaboration, and academic advancement. At the University of Maryland, you will have the resources and clinical complexity of a major academic medical center while also having the opportunity to make a visible and lasting contribution to the growth of our dermatopathology program. Our location in Baltimore, Maryland, places faculty in the heart of the Baltimore-Washington region, with convenient access to Washington, D.C., the Chesapeake Bay, major East Coast cities, and several major airports. We are looking for more than an outstanding diagnostician. We are looking for a colleague, educator, collaborator, and future leader who is excited about bringing a pathology perspective to an academic Department of Dermatology. If you are a Pathology-Trained Dermatopathologist looking for an academic environment where your expertise will be valued and where you can have a meaningful role in shaping the future of the program, we would like to hear from you. Compensation and Benefits Expected rank for this position will be Assistant Professor or higher, however, final rank and tenure status will be commensurate with selected candidate’s experience. Expected Salary Range: $210,000 to $320,000. The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the departmental faculty compensation program or pay from participation in departmental variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position offers a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. Note: Leave and tuition benefits are prorated for part-time employees. UMB is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. If you need a reasonable accommodation for a disability for any part of the employment process, please submit an online request or contact HRDiversity@umaryland.edu . Please note that only inquiries concerning a request for reasonable accommodation will be responded to from this email address . Candidates should submit a cover letter and a recent CV, including names and contact information of three references to Shawn Kwatra, MD, Chair, Department of Dermatology at Skwatra@som.umaryland.edu The University of Maryland School of Medicine (SOM) was chartered in 1807 as the first public medical school in the United States. It continues today as one of the fastest growing, top-tier biomedical research enterprises in the world. SOM is dedicated to providing excellence in biomedical education, basic and clinical research, quality patient care and service to improve the health of the citizens of Maryland and beyond. Candidates must possess: MD, DO, or equivalent medical degree. Residency training in Anatomic Pathology or Anatomic and Clinical Pathology (AP or AP/CP). Board certification or board eligibility in Pathology. Completion of an accredited Dermatopathology Fellowship. Board certification or board eligibility in Dermatopathology. Eligibility for medical licensure in the State of Maryland. Excellent diagnostic skills and a strong foundation in surgical pathology. A commitment to collaborative, high-quality patient care. An interest in teaching and mentoring residents, medical students, and other learners. An interest in contributing to the growth of an academic dermatopathology program. As a member of the Department of Dermatology, you will work closely with dermatologists and multidisciplinary colleagues throughout the University of Maryland Medical System, providing expert dermatopathology interpretation and valuable clinicopathologic correlation. The position offers opportunities to: Interpret a diverse and challenging spectrum of dermatopathology specimens within a major academic medical center. Provide expertise in the diagnosis of inflammatory, neoplastic, infectious, and other complex diseases of the skin. Collaborate directly with dermatologists and other specialists on challenging cases and clinicopathologic correlation. Help develop, strengthen, and expand dermatopathology services within the Department of Dermatology. Participate in dermatopathology conferences, case reviews, tumor boards, and multidisciplinary discussions. Educate and mentor dermatology residents, medical students, and other trainees. Participate in clinical research, publications, scholarly projects, and quality-improvement initiatives. Pursue academic and leadership opportunities based on individual experience, interests, and career goals. Contribute to the continued growth and academic mission of the University of Maryland Department of Dermatology."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/581": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - SOM Dermatology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/11/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The Department of Dermatology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine seeks to recruit a candidate for a full-time position in general medical dermatology. The successful candidate will join our Department of Dermatology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine and provide patient care and education within our residency training program. The Department of Dermatology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine seeks to recruit a candidate for a full-time position in general medical dermatology. The successful candidate will join our Department of Dermatology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine and provide patient care and education within our residency training program. The ideal candidate will have a strong interest both in practicing and teaching general dermatology as well as non-Mohs surgical dermatology. Particular areas of subspecialty interest might include inpatient consultative dermatology, complex medical dermatology, and/or dermatology of skin of color. A commitment to resident education is necessary. Expected rank is Assistant Professor/Associate Professor, however, rank and tenure status is dependent upon candidate’s qualifications. Qualified Candidate will have a strong interest in practicing clinical dermatology and be Board certified or eligible. Expected salary range for Assistant Professors is $284,466 (min) and $569,296 (max). The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the Dermatology faculty compensation program or pay from participation in Dermatology variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum (25%) and maximum (90%) salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. The University of Maryland, Baltimore and the University of Maryland School of Medicine are equal opportunity employers. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. We value diversity and how it enriches our academic and scientific community and strive toward cultivating an inclusive environment that supports all employees. Candidates should submit a Curriculum Vitae and a brief statement of interest to Shawn Kwatra, MD, Chair, Department of Dermatology at SKwatra@som.umaryland.edu Medical Doctor, Board Certified The appointee should also show potential for superior teaching, service, and research, scholarship, or creative performance, commensurate with the mission of the institution."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/582": {
      "title": "Dermatologist / Dermatopathologist - SOM Dermatology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/11/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The Department of Dermatology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is seeking a full-time Academic Dermatologist and Dermatopathologist to join its growing faculty. The Department of Dermatology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is seeking a full-time Academic Dermatologist and Dermatopathologist to join its growing faculty. The successful candidate will contribute to an integrated academic program committed to excellence in clinical care, dermatopathology, medical education, scholarship, and multidisciplinary collaboration. The faculty member will provide dermatopathology interpretation and consultation and may participate in clinical dermatology or another area of surgical pathology, depending on training, interests, and departmental needs. Faculty appointment and academic rank will be commensurate with the candidate's qualifications and experience. Expected rank for this position will be Assistant Professor or higher, however, final rank and tenure status will be commensurate with selected candidate’s experience. Expected Salary Range: $270,000 to $375,000. The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the departmental faculty compensation program or pay from participation in departmental variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position offers a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. Note: Leave and tuition benefits are prorated for part-time employees. UMB is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. If you need a reasonable accommodation for a disability for any part of the employment process, please submit an online request or contact HRDiversity@umaryland.edu. Please note that only inquiries concerning a request for reasonable accommodation will be responded to from this email address. Candidates should submit a cover letter and a recent CV, including names and contact information of three references to Shawn Kwatra, MD, Chair, Department of Dermatology at Skwatra@som.umaryland.edu The University of Maryland School of Medicine (SOM) was chartered in 1807 as the first public medical school in the United States. It continues today as one of the fastest growing, top-tier biomedical research enterprises in the world. SOM is dedicated to providing excellence in biomedical education, basic and clinical research, quality patient care and service to improve the health of the citizens of Maryland and beyond. Candidates must possess: - An MD, DO, or equivalent medical degree from an accredited institution. - Completion of an accredited residency in Dermatology or Anatomic Pathology/Anatomic and Clinical Pathology. - Completion of an accredited fellowship in Dermatopathology. - Board certification or board eligibility in Dermatopathology. - Board certification or board eligibility in the candidate's primary specialty, as applicable. - Eligibility for an unrestricted medical license in the State of Maryland. - Strong diagnostic, clinical, communication, and interpersonal skills. - A demonstrated commitment to high-quality patient care, education, teamwork, and academic collaboration. Preference may be given to candidates who demonstrate one or more of the following: - Experience in an academic medical center or high-volume dermatopathology practice. - Expertise in complex inflammatory skin disease, cutaneous oncology, cutaneous lymphoma, pediatric dermatopathology, alopecia, transplant dermatopathology, immunodermatology, or molecular diagnostics. - Experience with direct immunofluorescence, immunohistochemistry, molecular testing, or other ancillary diagnostic techniques. - Interest or additional training in a complementary surgical pathology subspecialty. - A record of teaching, mentorship, scholarly productivity, quality improvement, or clinical research. - Interest in developing collaborative clinical, educational, or translational research programs. Academic Environment The University of Maryland School of Medicine offers a highly collaborative academic environment with opportunities to work across departments, centers, and clinical programs. The successful candidate will join faculty dedicated to advancing dermatologic care, diagnostic excellence, professional education, and discovery. The position provides opportunities to: - Work with a broad and diverse case mix from general and subspecialty dermatology practices. - Collaborate with multidisciplinary clinical and research teams. - Teach learners at multiple levels, including medical students, residents, and fellows. - Develop an academic portfolio aligned with the candidate's interests and career goals. - Participate in clinical, translational, educational, and quality-improvement scholarship. - Help shape the strategic growth of dermatopathology services within a leading academic medical institution. - Provide expert interpretation of dermatologic biopsy and excision specimens using histopathologic, immunohistochemical, molecular, and other ancillary diagnostic methods as appropriate. - Produce accurate, comprehensive, and timely dermatopathology reports. - Offer subspecialty consultation and clinicopathologic correlation to dermatologists, pathologists, surgeons, oncologists, and other referring clinicians. - Participate in clinical dermatology or an additional pathology subspecialty, as appropriate to the candidate's background and the department's needs. - Educate and mentor medical students, residents, fellows, and other trainees through conferences, clinical instruction, case review, and didactic teaching. - Participate in multidisciplinary conferences and collaborate with faculty across dermatology, pathology and related specialties. - Contribute to quality assurance, laboratory improvement, regulatory compliance, and best practices in dermatopathology. - Engage in scholarly activity, including clinical or translational research, peer-reviewed publications, presentations, educational innovation, and quality-improvement initiatives. - Support the continued growth and development of dermatopathology services within the University of Maryland academic health system. - Participate in departmental, school, and institutional service appropriate to faculty rank."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/572": {
      "title": "Associate Professor - SOM Med Cardiology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States Pediatric Cardiologist Join the University of Maryland School of Medicine, Department of Pediatrics, Division of Pediatric Cardiology. As we grow our signature pediatric heart program, we are seeking an experienced interventional cardiologist at the Associate or Full Professor level to join our program. Pediatric Cardiologist Join the University of Maryland School of Medicine, Department of Pediatrics, Division of Pediatric Cardiology . As we grow our signature pediatric heart program , we are seeking an experienced interventional cardiologist at the Associate or Full Professor level to join our program. Expected rank for this position will be Associate Professor or higher, however, final rank and tenure status will be commensurate with selected candidate’s experience. The successful applicant must have an MD or MD and PhD degrees, or their equivalent. Candidates should have clinical training in Pediatrics and Pediatric Cardiology (completed fellowship and be board eligible or board certified). Preference will be given to candidates who have expertise in interventional cardiology (pediatric and adult congenital). Position Highlights: Superb working environment including 8 physicians and a group of NPs Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team and experts, including a world renowned pediatric cardiac surgeon, genetics, behavioral pediatrics and pediatric neurology and board certified adult congenital cardiologist Excellent collaborative research and leadership opportunities Strong inpatient and outpatient cardiology practice to include seven practice sites across the State of Maryland Features: Full spectrum of care from prenatal and birth to childhood and adulthood, all in one hospital State of the art Bi-Plane Philips Cath Lab configured for a full spectrum of procedures in pediatric congenital and adult congenital cardiac diagnostic and interventional procedures Full Pediatric Cardiac Anesthesia support State of the art 52-bed Level IV NICU– currently a U.S. News & World Report top 50 ranked Neonatal ICU! 19 bed PICU with dedicated cardiac PICU beds 6 bed IMC 29 full service general pediatric beds 20 bed Pediatric Emergency Department Full ECMO support facility at University of Maryland Children’s Hospital Academic Faculty Position in the University of Maryland School of Medicine, with teaching responsibilities for medical students and pediatric residents Benefits/Perks: Very generous leave package Dependent tuition remission for any school within the University of Maryland system Excellent pension/retirement plans Types of insurance coverage offered include: life, disability, liability Very competitive salary with bonus opportunity, as well as opportunities for academic promotion, research collaboration, and outreach The University of Maryland Children's Hospital (UMCH) has a renowned Children’s Heart Program with dedicated cardiac PICU beds. We have recently expanded our critical care, neurology, and neonatology services providing opportunities for career development. We are also home to a pioneering artificial blood clinical research program. The University of Maryland Golisano Children’s Hospital, named in recognition of a historic $50 million-dollar philanthropic investment, is part of the Golisano Children’s Alliance, a national network of premier pediatric hospitals. This investment expands our clinical programs, pediatric research, and innovation. Our hospital benefits from enhanced collaboration, sharing clinical expertise, research insights, and educational opportunities as part of the Golisano Children’s Alliance to drive continuous improvement in pediatric care. We are located near the downtown Inner Harbor area, just one of Baltimore’s many outstanding attractions. From fine arts and orchestras to professional sports teams, first-class dining, and shopping to a wealth of historical sites, our city offers a full range of recreational and cultural opportunities. Washington, D.C., Philadelphia, and New York City are within easy reach, as well as beaches to the east and mountains to the west. Educational excellence abounds, as do family-friendly neighborhoods and urban living options. Visit us online at www.ummsphysician.jobs to learn more. Refer to Position # 03-314-569 Salary range: $400,000 - $475,000 The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. UMB is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. If you need a reasonable accommodation for a disability for any part of the employment process, please submit an online request or contact HRDiversity@umaryland.edu. Please note that only inquiries concerning a request for reasonable accommodation will be responded to from this email address. The University of Maryland School of Medicine (SOM) was chartered in 1807 as the first public medical school in the United States. It continues today as one of the fastest growing, top-tier biomedical research enterprises in the world. SOM is dedicated to providing excellence in biomedical education, basic and clinical research, quality patient care and service to improve the health of the citizens of Maryland and beyond. Doctorate or recognized terminal degree in the field of specialization. Successful experience in teaching and research, scholarship, or creative performance, and, when appropriate to the mission of the UMB, be competent to offer graduate instruction and direct graduate research. There shall also be evidence of relevant and effective service to the institution, the community, and the profession. May require unrestricted license in the State of Maryland. The appointee ordinarily shall have had successful experience in teaching and research, scholarship, or creative performance, and, when appropriate to the mission of the institution, be competent to offer graduate instruction and direct graduate research. There shall also be evidence of relevant and effective service to the institution, the community, and the profession."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/568": {
      "title": "Non-Adjunct Faculty - SOM Diagnostic Radiology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Adjunct Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States General/Multispecialty Radiologist – Become Part of Something Amazing! Institution: University of Maryland School of Medicine Primary Practice Site: UM Shore Regional Health (Eastern Shore of Maryland) Salary Range: $500,000–$600,000+ (commensurate with experience and productivity) Position Overview The Department of Radiology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is recruiting three multispecialty radiologists to support UM Shore Regional Health, with hybrid on-site and remote work. Onsite work is primarily at our Easton, MD location – although other locations on the Maryland eastern Shore are available. These positions are designed for general radiology with a flexible subspecialty focus if desired by the candidate. The clinical work consists of a fulfilling and balanced mix of XR, US, CT, MR, and fluoroscopy with a collegial team. We have a longstanding legacy of excellence and offer: A highly competitive compensation plan with performance-based incentives (pay per RVU above a baseline amount). A strong emphasis on radiologist flexibility in schedules and staffing: various schedule options including typical schedules, 7on7off, 2 weeks on (5-day workweeks) followed by 1 week off, etc. Contact us for further details. Outstanding colleagues in a supportive, collaborative environment; integrate with our large multispecialty radiology group based in Baltimore (who also provide onsite services). The position can be tailored to accommodate your schedule as a per diem contractor. Enjoy an Exceptional Lifestyle on Maryland’s Eastern Shore Join our team at UM Shore Regional Health and enjoy the unmatched quality of life on Maryland’s Eastern Shore. Easton is a scenic, waterfront community known for safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, vibrant arts, and year-round outdoor recreation. Physicians may choose to live locally or commute from Annapolis , just ~40 minutes away. Annapolis offers historic charm, top-tier dining, strong schools, and easy access to Baltimore, Washington, DC, and major airports —an ideal home base for those seeking coastal living with metropolitan amenities. This opportunity combines a supportive clinical environment with a relaxed, family-friendly lifestyle in one of the Mid-Atlantic’s most desirable regions. Contact Faculty rank and radiologist salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. For more details or to express interest, please email and attach your CV and any specific interests or questions. tarek.hanna@umm.edu The University of Maryland, Baltimore is an Equal Opportunity, Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law or policy. We value diversity and how it enriches our academic and scientific community and strive toward cultivating an inclusive environment that supports all employees. Expertise in the discipline and recognition for accomplishment sufficient to gain the endorsement of the preponderance of the members of the faculty of the department to which he or she is appointed. Faculty members at the University who are: Appointed to provide contractually defined responsibilities such as research, service, or instruction for non-credit bearing courses; Neither tenured nor eligible for tenure;"
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/589": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow A",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/11/2026 Category: Fellow JobFunction: Post Doctoral Fellow JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: MD, United States The University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB), Center for Vaccine Development and Global Health (CVD) brings together more than four decades of innovative and life-saving research on vaccines and infectious diseases. http:// www.medschool.umaryland.edu/cvd/. The University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB), Center for Vaccine Development and Global Health (CVD) brings together more than four decades of innovative and life-saving research on vaccines and infectious diseases. http:// www.medschool.umaryland.edu/cvd/ . The malaria research laboratory of Prof. Stefan H. I. Kappe at the Center for Vaccine Development and Global Health (CVD), University of Maryland School of Medicine, is recruiting a highly motivated Postdoctoral Fellow to investigate the immune mechanisms of protection against malaria infection mediated by vaccination. The Kappe laboratory has pioneered the development of genetically attenuated malaria parasites (GAPs) and whole-sporozoite malaria vaccines designed to induce durable protective immunity against Plasmodium infection. Our research combines cutting-edge immunology, parasite biology, and translational vaccine development to understand how liver-stage malaria parasites interact with the host immune system, identify protective immune mechanisms and novel antigen targets, and define immune correlates of protection. Ongoing projects span basic immunology, systems biology, controlled human malaria infection (CHMI) studies, and clinical malaria vaccine development. This position offers an exceptional opportunity to join a collaborative, multidisciplinary research program dedicated to advancing next-generation malaria vaccines while providing outstanding scientific mentorship and career development. Research Areas Research projects may include: Vaccine-induced CD8⁺ and CD4⁺ T-cell immunity Innate immune regulation of adaptive responses Immune correlates of protection against malaria Identification of protective malaria antigens Regulatory T-cell and inflammatory responses during infection Systems immunology and high-dimensional immune profiling Single-cell transcriptomics and T-cell receptor (TCR) repertoire analysis Translational studies supporting human malaria vaccine clinical trials Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Immunology, Microbiology, Infectious Diseases, Parasitology, or a closely related discipline. Strong background in cellular and molecular immunology, with demonstrated expertise in adaptive and/or innate immune responses. Hands-on experience with immunological techniques, including multiparameter flow cytometry, immune cell isolation, cell culture, and functional immune assays. Experience working with infectious disease models and/or animal models of infection and vaccination. Demonstrated ability to independently design, execute, troubleshoot, and interpret complex experiments. Excellent analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills with meticulous attention to detail. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including a record of scientific publications in peer-reviewed journals. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Design, develop, and execute independent and collaborative research projects investigating immune mechanisms underlying malaria infection and vaccine-induced protection. Perform advanced immunological experiments, including multiparameter flow cytometry, cell sorting, ELISA, ELISpot, intracellular cytokine staining, immune cell culture, cytotoxicity assays, and other functional immune assays. Apply and interpret high-dimensional immune profiling approaches, including spectral flow cytometry, mass cytometry (CyTOF), single-cell RNA sequencing, and T-cell receptor (TCR) repertoire analyses. Analyze complex immunological datasets using FlowJo, R, RStudio, and other statistical or bioinformatics tools to identify immune correlates of protection and mechanisms of vaccine-induced immunity. Investigate host-parasite interactions during liver-stage malaria infection using in vitro and in vivo experimental models. Contribute to studies evaluating immune responses induced by genetically attenuated parasite (GAP) vaccines, whole-sporozoite vaccines, and controlled human malaria infection (CHMI) studies. Design, optimize, troubleshoot, and document experimental protocols while maintaining accurate laboratory records and ensuring scientific rigor and reproducibility. Prepare manuscripts for publication, scientific presentations, fellowship applications, and contribute to grant proposals. Mentor graduate students, research technicians, and undergraduate trainees while fostering a collaborative and inclusive research environment. Collaborate effectively with multidisciplinary teams across immunology, molecular parasitology, bioinformatics, systems biology, and clinical research. Present research findings at laboratory meetings, institutional seminars, and national and international scientific conferences. Maintain compliance with institutional biosafety, animal care, laboratory safety, and research regulations."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/594": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor - SOD AOST Dental Hygiene (.90 FTE) (186237)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Clin Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) invites applications for a .90 FTE clinical-track faculty position as a Clinical Assistant Professor in the Department of Advanced Oral Sciences and Therapeutics, dental hygiene program. The University of Maryland School of Dentistry (UMSOD) is the world's first dental college and Maryland’s predominant provider of comprehensive and emergency oral health services for individuals of all ages, including the underserved and disadvantaged. Through research innovation, creativity, and productive partnerships, our faculty, staff, and students are developing and implementing novel approaches to advance oral health and improve lives. Applicants must possess a Bachelor of Science in dental hygiene. Energetic applicants with a positive attitude towards teaching and a desire to develop and advance in a career in dental education are preferred. • Master’s degree preferred The position will be available until filled. Interested applicants should submit a, (1) current, signed and dated curriculum vitae, (2) a detailed letter addressing the criteria for hiring stated above, and (3) three letters of recommendation. Hiring range: $75,600 - $81,000 per year (depending on academic rank and commensurate with education and experience). Primary responsibilities include teaching clinical and didactic dental hygiene, leading the Clinical Dental Hygiene Leader program, participation in scholarly activities, engage in externally funded scholarships, community-engaged academic work, admissions to include application review, and interviews, and service to the organization."
    }
  },
